timeline.message:
Extract SourceType from VideoPlaybackResolver and return it in MediaItemTags

Know the SourceType of the current content instead of the latest resolved one ensures to apply properly the seamless transition for the good content, and will also ensure no conflicts between quality selection of manifest sources (not only for livestreams, even if playback from a "master" manifest URL is only used for livestreams currently) and the one of videos.

The SourceType enum has been moved from VideoPlaybackResolver to a separate enum and its values have been refactored: instead of LIVE_STREAM, VIDEO_WITH_SEPARATED_AUDIO, VIDEO_WITH_AUDIO_OR_AUDIO_ONLY values, the following values are now present:

- UNKNOWN, used when the SourceType is not known yet or is not applicable (for ExceptionTag and PlaceHolderTag in this case);

- MANIFEST, for sources which are not generated from AudioStreams and VideoStreams, but instead from DASH and HLS URLs returned by StreamExtractors and StreamInfos;

- VIDEO_WITH_SEPARATED_AUDIO, for sources generated from VideoStreams which are video-only with a separated AudioStream;

- VIDEO_ONLY, for sources generated from VideoStreams which are video-only, and this without an audio external source;

- VIDEO_WITH_AUDIO, for sources generated from VideoStreams which are not video-only;

- AUDIO_ONLY, for sources generated from AudioStreams only.

A new getter has been added in MediaItemTag, getSourceType(), which returns the SourceType of the content. The interface has a default implementation returning the UNKNOWN value.

Because a MediaItemTag is built before knowing the SourceType, the property cannot be set in the constructor: that's the reason why a setter has been added for this value in StreamInfoTag, setSourceType(SourceType), and that the getter method has been overridden in this class.

As a side effect, StreamInfoTags created in Resolvers are not downcasted to the interface anymore, in order to set the SourceType when we know it. The corresponding attribute in StreamInfoTag, sourceType, is always initialized with the UNKNOWN value, in order to ensure non-nullability of the attribute, and so of the corresponding getter return.

